[00:56.10] We wept as we passed through the mountains clothed in July clouds,
[01:22.76] under the restraint of power lines, their fury bursting through the summer haze as ethereal music filled the air.
[01:48.66] Nearly conquered by the mountain, I have found such deep respect for what you destroy.
[02:07.50] Older than time and cut down by a lesser foe, like thieves in the night mined for coal.
[02:46.72] Timeless stone buried beneath, unearthing the secret poisons into its belly...
[03:07.46] You hack at the mountain and scrape away for your simple need what was formed by silent gods on the day the void first burst with sound.
[03:52.98] Pulsing with life, you don't see its shimmering green.
[04:01.02] You see the deeps hue of coal, grey smoke and black waters in the stream...
[04:08.64] Poison the earth, poison the stream, killing the weary giants as they sleep, blackened waters, sand and soot-grinding gears halt serenity.
